        <div class="card" style="margin-top:1.5rem">
          <h2 style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:1.2rem;font-weight:700;margin-bottom:1rem">How to calculate avocado calories</h2>
          <p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:0.9rem;line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:0.75rem">If you know the edible weight of your avocado, estimating its calories is straightforward. Using the reference value of 160 kcal per 100g, multiply the weight in grams by 1.6.</p>
          <p style="font-size:0.95rem;line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:0.75rem"><strong>Calories = avocado weight in grams × 1.6</strong></p>
          <p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:0.9rem;line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:0.75rem">For example, 75g of avocado contains approximately 120 calories, while 150g contains around 240 calories. This calculation uses the edible flesh only, not the skin or stone.</p>
          <p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:0.9rem;line-height:1.8">If you are making guacamole or avocado toast, remember to include the other ingredients separately. Bread, oil, cheese and other additions can significantly increase the total calories in the meal.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <aside class="calc-sidebar">
        <div class="card sidebar-card">
          <h2>How much avocado should you eat?</h2>
          <p>There is no single recommended daily amount that suits everyone. A portion of around 50–100g can be a practical starting point, depending on your appetite, energy needs and the rest of your diet. Since avocado is relatively calorie-dense, weighing a portion can help if you are tracking your calorie intake.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card sidebar-card">
          <h3>Frequently asked questions</h3>
          <details>
            <summary>How many calories are in half an avocado?</summary>
            <p>It depends on the size. Half a small avocado containing around 75g of flesh provides approximately 120 calories. Half a medium avocado containing 100g provides around 160 calories.</p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>How many calories are in a whole avocado?</summary>
            <p>A whole avocado provides different amounts depending on its edible weight. Using 160 kcal per 100g, a small avocado with 100g of flesh has around 160 calories, while a medium avocado with 150g has around 240 calories.</p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>Is avocado good for weight loss?</summary>
            <p>Avocado can fit into a weight-management plan. It contains fibre and unsaturated fats, but it is also relatively high in calories. Whether it supports your goal depends on portion size and your overall eating pattern, rather than on one food alone.</p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>How many calories are in avocado toast?</summary>
            <p>The total depends on the bread and the amount of avocado. For example, one slice of bread containing 130–150 calories with 50g of avocado containing around 80 calories would provide approximately 210–230 calories before any extra toppings.</p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>Does avocado contain protein?</summary>
            <p>Yes, but not a large amount compared with foods such as eggs, fish, beans or tofu. Avocado contains approximately 2g of protein per 100g and is better known for its unsaturated fats and fibre.</p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>Is avocado high in carbohydrates?</summary>
            <p>Avocado contains around 8.5g of total carbohydrates per 100g, including approximately 6.7g of fibre in these reference values. The amount of digestible carbohydrate is therefore lower than the total carbohydrate figure.</p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>Do I weigh an avocado with or without the stone?</summary>
            <p>For the most accurate estimate, weigh the edible flesh after removing the skin and stone. This calculator uses the weight of the flesh only.</p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>Are avocado calories the same in guacamole?</summary>
            <p>Not necessarily. Plain mashed avocado has a similar nutritional profile to avocado flesh, but guacamole often contains other ingredients such as tomato, onion, lime juice or oil. Its calories per 100g depend on the recipe.</p>
          </details>
